From: Gyimesi Balázs <gyimesi.balazs@gmail.com>
Subject: nss-gmac: set max_mtu

The netdev max_mtu stays at the ether_setup() default of 1500, so the
jumbo support of ndo_change_mtu cannot be used, and a DSA switch behind
the GMAC cannot raise the conduit MTU for its tag. Allow up to the
driver's jumbo limit.

--- a/ipq806x/nss_gmac_ctrl.c
+++ b/ipq806x/nss_gmac_ctrl.c
@@ -1383,6 +1383,10 @@
 
 	netdev->watchdog_timeo = 5 * HZ;
 	netdev->netdev_ops = &nss_gmac_netdev_ops;
+	/* ndo_change_mtu handles jumbo frames; a DSA switch behind the
+	 * GMAC also needs room for its tag on top of a full frame
+	 */
+	netdev->max_mtu = NSS_GMAC_JUMBO_MTU;
 	nss_gmac_ethtool_register(netdev);
 
 	/*
